    "abstract": "We report the first detailed investigation of K2MnS2 and K2MnSe2 from the K2MnS2 structure type and their magnetic solid solution K2MnS2 −x Se x and find that compounds of this structure type consist of strongly-coupled pseudo-one-dimensional antiferromagnetic chains that collectively represent a frustrated two-dimensional triangular antiferromagnet. Bulk samples of K2MnS2 −x Se x with 0 ≤ x ≤ 2 are characterized using X-ray diffraction, neutron diffraction, magnetization and heat capacity measurements. An incommensurate cycloid magnetic structure with a magnetic propagation vector k = [0 . 58 0 1] is observed for all samples in K2MnS2 −x Se x , and the ordering is robust despite a 12% increase in cell volume. Geometric frustration of chains results in incommensurability along a and a two-step magnetic transition. The varying geometries accessible in compounds of this structure type are presented as promising avenues to tune frustration.",
